<title>SPAIN: Spain says labour reform to be finalised in 1997.</title>
<headline>Spain says labour reform to be finalised in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government's labour market reform will be finalised in 1997 and meetings with trade unions will start in the fourth quarter of this year, Labour Minister Javier Arenas told journalists on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The government is conscious that it must face a reform of the labour market in 1997,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Arenas said the fall in social security contributions that employers are calling for should be negotiated by way of pensions agreement known as the Toledo Pact, rather than as part of the reform of the labour market.</p>
<p>The Labour Ministry's National Employment Institute INEM will have a budget of 1.9 trillion pesetas in 1997, 80 percent of which will go towards paying unemployment benefits.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
